			<div class="content" id="post-content-4519462">
									

<p>These are my thoughts (hopefully they mean something):</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">spoilers?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">warned&nbsp;you.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The Conprocs and Description did not impress me. The only notable thing that made me have any sort of reaction was the plug in the spine (which, by the way. gross.) It might've just been me but how it was laid out and presented didnt really make sense for me. I actually really enjoy the Arcadia GoI so far as it stands, but how its described felt&#8230; unnecessary? The extra information also confused me a bit, but really that might be me.</p>
<p>In terms of narrative, <em>eh</em>? The base concept for it just feels a bit tropey. &quot;Whoa look, these guys are stuck in a VR game <em>whoaaa!</em>&quot; was the only thing I could really think of while reading. Nolan as a character seemed interesting, but it was a little overshadowed by the PoI's unnatural dialogue. Like, I understand what hes supposed to be, but his interactions/attitude felt really overdone.</p>
<p>For the listed reasons I have to give it a -1. Theres some other things, but I'm having trouble finding the words. The entire concept just feels weak, and the associated narrative doesnt really justify it enough for me.</p>
<p><strong>EDIT:</strong> After looking at the final Addendum, I realize that it (talking about that final Addendum) does have potential. But, I just feel like it's not too widely explored. I actually almost forget it existed until I looked through the skip again. I really wish that was more explored, as that seems like an interesting enough twist for the story and concept.</p>
</div>
