			<div class="content" id="post-content-4759761">
									

<p>This one doesn't really grab me. Narrative-wise it's decent, but the &quot;high-as-donkey-balls programmers trying to save a dying console company&quot; topic doesn't go up my alley.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Tone/formatting/grammar/other&nbsp;issues</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Person of Interest #1377 is currently housed within Site-107</p>
</blockquote>
<p>however, in the interview, he's referred to as PoI-1137</p>
<blockquote>
<p>DNA testing of the tissue located within SCP-1926 has not been fruitful to date</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;fruitful&quot; doesn't sound clinical, you could use &quot;successful&quot;, or &quot;DNA testing of the tissue has been inconclusive&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>and an cable of unknown purpose or design surgically attached to SCP-1926-A and SCP-1926-B's spines</p>
</blockquote>
<p>besides the &quot;an cable&quot; issue, &quot;spines&quot; should be replaced with &quot;vertebral columns&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>PoI-1137 was arrested after police attempted to issue an in-person fine. Subsequently, law enforcement entered the home and discovered PoI-1137</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This sounds like the police arrested him, then entered his home and found him there <em>again</em></p>
<p>Having the last 2 interviews in collapsibles is good, but having the first one (which is also longer than the other 2) as-is isn't consistent, I'd put that too in a collapsible</p>
<p>And then there's the interviews' content, which really seems like they're trying too hard, have excessive amounts of colloquialisms, and are pretty incoherent overall.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It's nasty, covered to the BRIM with teeth and hair and shit… no, not like, poopy</p>
</blockquote>
<p>is pretty unnecessary and doesn't add anything. There's more phrases like this one tho</p>
<blockquote>
<p>But apparently the powers that be thought that was too grandiose</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I can't figure out what this means</p>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Close</a></div>
</div>
</div>
<p>The incident report has potential, but it doesn't make up for everything else. Overall -1, but if this sees some work I'll reconsider</p>

							</div>

								
					
